# Personal notes: learning log, working documents, AI assistant config.
# These are for me, not for anyone reading the repository.
#
# Design documents stay tracked on purpose — docs/adr/ and the schema/API
# design notes explain why the system looks the way it does, which is the
# part worth publishing.
CLAUDE.md
LEARNING_ROADMAP.md
PROJECT_RULES.md
DEVELOPMENT_WORKFLOW.md
docs/ANNOTATIONS.md
docs/GLOSSARY.md
docs/PROJECT_STATE.md
docs/HANDS_OFF_DAY*.md
docs/REVIEW_DAY*.md
docs/SYSTEM_OVERVIEW.md
docs/TODO.md
docs/LOCAL_SETUP.md

# Maven build output
target/

# IntelliJ IDEA
.idea/
*.iml
*.iws
*.ipr

# VS Code
.vscode/

# OS cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Logs
*.log
logs/

# Secrets. Never commit.
#
# .env.example is the exception: it holds placeholder values only and is
# what tells a new developer which variables they need.
.env
.env.local
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# Local-only overrides
application-local.yml
application-local.yaml

# Gradle, if it is ever used
.gradle/
build/

# Scratch payloads for manual API testing
#
# They contain real tokens and passwords. Examples worth keeping belong in
# docs/ with placeholder values.
/*.json
